{"key":"nlp-basics-u2-05","seriesId":"nlp-basics","episode":"u2-05","title":"Hidden Markov Models, Intuitively","fps":30,"duration":220.087,"durationInFrames":6603,"video":{"width":1920,"height":1080,"burnCaptions":true,"brand":"learnvi.in"},"badge":["UNIT 2 · LESSON 5","HIDDEN MARKOV MODELS"],"series":{"title":"NLP, Simply Explained","subtitle":"University NLP, one idea at a time, no heavy maths","runningPrompt":"","stops":[{"id":"u1-01","number":1,"name":"The Stages of NLP: From Letters to Meaning","stamp":"THE STAGES OF NLP: FROM LETTERS TO MEANING","topic":""},{"id":"u1-02","number":2,"name":"Tokenization: How Text Becomes Pieces","stamp":"TOKENIZATION: HOW TEXT BECOMES PIECES","topic":""},{"id":"u1-03","number":3,"name":"Text Classification: Teaching Computers to Sort Text","stamp":"TEXT CLASSIFICATION: TEACHING COMPUTERS TO SORT TEXT","topic":""},{"id":"u1-04","number":4,"name":"Language Models: Guessing the Next Word","stamp":"LANGUAGE MODELS: GUESSING THE NEXT WORD","topic":""},{"id":"u2-01","number":5,"name":"Morphology: The Building Blocks Inside Words","stamp":"MORPHOLOGY: THE BUILDING BLOCKS INSIDE WORDS","topic":""},{"id":"u2-02","number":6,"name":"Part-of-Speech Tagging: Is It a Noun or a Verb?","stamp":"PART-OF-SPEECH TAGGING: IS IT A NOUN OR A VERB?","topic":""},{"id":"u2-03","number":7,"name":"Chunking: Grouping Words into Phrases","stamp":"CHUNKING: GROUPING WORDS INTO PHRASES","topic":""},{"id":"u2-04","number":8,"name":"Generative vs Discriminative Models","stamp":"GENERATIVE VS DISCRIMINATIVE MODELS","topic":""},{"id":"u2-05","number":9,"name":"Hidden Markov Models, Intuitively","stamp":"HIDDEN MARKOV MODELS, INTUITIVELY","topic":""},{"id":"u2-06","number":10,"name":"Conditional Random Fields, Intuitively","stamp":"CONDITIONAL RANDOM FIELDS, INTUITIVELY","topic":""},{"id":"u3-01","number":11,"name":"Constituency Parsing: Sentences as Trees","stamp":"CONSTITUENCY PARSING: SENTENCES AS TREES","topic":""},{"id":"u3-02","number":12,"name":"Dependency Parsing: Who Did What to Whom","stamp":"DEPENDENCY PARSING: WHO DID WHAT TO WHOM","topic":""},{"id":"u3-03","number":13,"name":"Transition-Based Parsing: Building Trees Step by Step","stamp":"TRANSITION-BASED PARSING: BUILDING TREES STEP BY STEP","topic":""},{"id":"u4-01","number":14,"name":"Word Vectors: Giving Words a Place on a Map","stamp":"WORD VECTORS: GIVING WORDS A PLACE ON A MAP","topic":""},{"id":"u4-02","number":15,"name":"Word2Vec: Learning Word Vectors from Context","stamp":"WORD2VEC: LEARNING WORD VECTORS FROM CONTEXT","topic":""},{"id":"u4-03","number":16,"name":"Recurrent Neural Networks: Reading with Memory","stamp":"RECURRENT NEURAL NETWORKS: READING WITH MEMORY","topic":""},{"id":"u4-04","number":17,"name":"LSTMs: Remembering What Matters","stamp":"LSTMS: REMEMBERING WHAT MATTERS","topic":""},{"id":"u5-01","number":18,"name":"Contextual Embeddings and ELMo","stamp":"CONTEXTUAL EMBEDDINGS AND ELMO","topic":""},{"id":"u5-02","number":19,"name":"BERT: Reading in Both Directions","stamp":"BERT: READING IN BOTH DIRECTIONS","topic":""}]},"stop":{"number":9,"name":"Hidden Markov Models, Intuitively","stamp":"HIDDEN MARKOV MODELS, INTUITIVELY"},"shorts":{"width":1080,"height":1920,"maxSeconds":60,"cta":"Full lesson: NLP, Simply Explained · Unit 2"},"thumbnail":{"headline":"How AI guesses hidden tags","big":"hidden tags"},"segments":[{"id":"intro","kind":"intro","component":"TitleCard","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c01","start":0.6,"end":7.061,"marks":{},"text":"Welcome back to NLP, Simply Explained. This is unit 2, lesson 5: hidden Markov models.","words":[{"w":"Welcome","start":0.6},{"w":"back","start":1.08},{"w":"to","start":1.427},{"w":"NLP,","start":1.773},{"w":"Simply","start":2.12},{"w":"Explained.","start":2.8},{"w":"This","start":3.6},{"w":"is","start":3.88},{"w":"unit","start":4.12},{"w":"2,","start":4.48},{"w":"lesson","start":4.84},{"w":"5:","start":5.2},{"w":"hidden","start":5.64},{"w":"Markov","start":6.08},{"w":"models.","start":6.52}]},{"id":"c02","start":7.461,"end":16.961,"marks":{},"text":"We've seen that a tagger has to work out whether each word is a noun, a verb, and so on. Today we meet the classic model that does it, without a single formula.","words":[{"w":"We've","start":7.461},{"w":"seen","start":7.701},{"w":"that","start":7.941},{"w":"a","start":8.061},{"w":"tagger","start":8.341},{"w":"has","start":8.621},{"w":"to","start":8.781},{"w":"work","start":8.941},{"w":"out","start":9.181},{"w":"whether","start":9.381},{"w":"each","start":9.701},{"w":"word","start":9.981},{"w":"is","start":10.261},{"w":"a","start":10.421},{"w":"noun,","start":10.581},{"w":"a","start":10.981},{"w":"verb,","start":11.381},{"w":"and","start":11.781},{"w":"so","start":12.021},{"w":"on.","start":12.301},{"w":"Today","start":12.841},{"w":"we","start":13.381},{"w":"meet","start":13.621},{"w":"the","start":13.861},{"w":"classic","start":13.981},{"w":"model","start":14.421},{"w":"that","start":14.781},{"w":"does","start":14.981},{"w":"it,","start":15.221},{"w":"without","start":15.501},{"w":"a","start":15.781},{"w":"single","start":15.941},{"w":"formula.","start":16.381}]}],"title":"Welcome","shortTitle":"Welcome","props":{"kicker":"Unit 2 · Lesson 5","title":"Hidden Markov Models","subtitle":"Guessing what you can't see"},"start":0.6,"end":16.961,"startFrame":0,"durationInFrames":536},{"id":"idea","kind":"core","component":"BigIdea","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c03","start":17.867,"end":28.66,"marks":{},"text":"Here's the idea. When we read text, we can see the words, but the tags are hidden. A hidden Markov model, or HMM, guesses the hidden tags from the words it can see.","words":[{"w":"Here's","start":17.867},{"w":"the","start":18.227},{"w":"idea.","start":18.427},{"w":"When","start":19.067},{"w":"we","start":19.307},{"w":"read","start":19.507},{"w":"text,","start":19.787},{"w":"we","start":20.307},{"w":"can","start":20.507},{"w":"see","start":20.667},{"w":"the","start":20.867},{"w":"words,","start":21.067},{"w":"but","start":21.427},{"w":"the","start":21.547},{"w":"tags","start":21.707},{"w":"are","start":22.147},{"w":"hidden.","start":22.347},{"w":"A","start":22.987},{"w":"hidden","start":23.227},{"w":"Markov","start":23.707},{"w":"model,","start":24.187},{"w":"or","start":24.747},{"w":"HMM,","start":25.307},{"w":"guesses","start":25.867},{"w":"the","start":26.427},{"w":"hidden","start":26.587},{"w":"tags","start":26.947},{"w":"from","start":27.387},{"w":"the","start":27.547},{"w":"words","start":27.667},{"w":"it","start":27.987},{"w":"can","start":28.147},{"w":"see.","start":28.387}]}],"title":"The big idea","shortTitle":"The big idea","props":{"kicker":"Key idea","text":"We can see the words. The tags are hidden. An HMM guesses the hidden tags from what it sees.","highlight":["hidden.","hidden"]},"start":17.867,"end":28.66,"startFrame":536,"durationInFrames":351},{"id":"hmm","kind":"core","component":"Definition","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c04","start":29.567,"end":38.354,"marks":{},"text":"A hidden Markov model imagines that hidden states, like part-of-speech tags, produce the things we observe, like words, one step at a time.","words":[{"w":"A","start":29.567},{"w":"hidden","start":29.687},{"w":"Markov","start":30.107},{"w":"model","start":30.527},{"w":"imagines","start":30.927},{"w":"that","start":31.607},{"w":"hidden","start":31.807},{"w":"states,","start":32.207},{"w":"like","start":32.727},{"w":"part-of-speech","start":33.267},{"w":"tags,","start":33.807},{"w":"produce","start":34.447},{"w":"the","start":34.927},{"w":"things","start":35.087},{"w":"we","start":35.407},{"w":"observe,","start":35.647},{"w":"like","start":36.247},{"w":"words,","start":36.527},{"w":"one","start":37.007},{"w":"step","start":37.327},{"w":"at","start":37.687},{"w":"a","start":37.847},{"w":"time.","start":38.007}]},{"id":"c05","start":38.754,"end":45.538,"marks":{},"text":"For \"the dog barks\", the hidden tags are determiner, noun, verb. What we see are just the words: the, dog, barks.","words":[{"w":"For","start":38.754},{"w":"\"the","start":38.914},{"w":"dog","start":39.074},{"w":"barks\",","start":39.394},{"w":"the","start":39.794},{"w":"hidden","start":39.994},{"w":"tags","start":40.354},{"w":"are","start":40.754},{"w":"determiner,","start":40.914},{"w":"noun,","start":41.474},{"w":"verb.","start":42.034},{"w":"What","start":42.594},{"w":"we","start":42.914},{"w":"see","start":43.074},{"w":"are","start":43.314},{"w":"just","start":43.474},{"w":"the","start":43.714},{"w":"words:","start":43.874},{"w":"the,","start":44.314},{"w":"dog,","start":44.554},{"w":"barks.","start":44.954}]},{"id":"c06","start":45.938,"end":55.58,"marks":{},"text":"Think of a friend's diary that never mentions the weather, only whether they carried an umbrella. You can't see the weather, but you can make a very good guess from the umbrellas.","words":[{"w":"Think","start":45.938},{"w":"of","start":46.138},{"w":"a","start":46.258},{"w":"friend's","start":46.418},{"w":"diary","start":46.818},{"w":"that","start":47.298},{"w":"never","start":47.498},{"w":"mentions","start":47.778},{"w":"the","start":48.258},{"w":"weather,","start":48.418},{"w":"only","start":48.978},{"w":"whether","start":49.298},{"w":"they","start":49.618},{"w":"carried","start":49.858},{"w":"an","start":50.038},{"w":"umbrella.","start":50.218},{"w":"You","start":51.218},{"w":"can't","start":51.538},{"w":"see","start":51.938},{"w":"the","start":52.138},{"w":"weather,","start":52.298},{"w":"but","start":52.698},{"w":"you","start":52.898},{"w":"can","start":53.098},{"w":"make","start":53.298},{"w":"a","start":53.458},{"w":"very","start":53.618},{"w":"good","start":53.858},{"w":"guess","start":54.098},{"w":"from","start":54.498},{"w":"the","start":54.859},{"w":"umbrellas.","start":55.219}]}],"title":"What is an HMM?","shortTitle":"What is an HMM?","props":{"kicker":"Definition","term":"Hidden Markov Model","definition":"A model where hidden states, like tags, produce the things we observe, like words, one step at a time.","example":"hidden: DET → NOUN → VERB  ·  seen: the dog barks","analogy":"Guessing the weather from a friend's diary that only says whether they carried an umbrella."},"start":29.567,"end":55.58,"startFrame":887,"durationInFrames":808},{"id":"two","kind":"core","component":"Compare","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c07","start":56.5,"end":61.331,"marks":{},"text":"An HMM learns just two kinds of chances, both by counting tagged text.","words":[{"w":"An","start":56.793},{"w":"HMM","start":57.087},{"w":"learns","start":57.38},{"w":"just","start":57.78},{"w":"two","start":57.98},{"w":"kinds","start":58.22},{"w":"of","start":58.46},{"w":"chances,","start":58.62},{"w":"both","start":59.3},{"w":"by","start":59.7},{"w":"counting","start":59.94},{"w":"tagged","start":60.34},{"w":"text.","start":60.74}]},{"id":"c08","start":61.731,"end":69.354,"marks":{},"text":"Transition chances: how likely one tag is to follow another. After a determiner like \"the\", a noun is very likely.","words":[{"w":"Transition","start":61.731},{"w":"chances:","start":62.451},{"w":"how","start":63.131},{"w":"likely","start":63.411},{"w":"one","start":63.851},{"w":"tag","start":64.091},{"w":"is","start":64.531},{"w":"to","start":64.691},{"w":"follow","start":64.851},{"w":"another.","start":65.251},{"w":"After","start":65.851},{"w":"a","start":66.211},{"w":"determiner","start":66.291},{"w":"like","start":66.971},{"w":"\"the\",","start":67.331},{"w":"a","start":67.691},{"w":"noun","start":67.891},{"w":"is","start":68.291},{"w":"very","start":68.531},{"w":"likely.","start":68.851}]},{"id":"c09","start":69.754,"end":76.273,"marks":{},"text":"Emission chances: how likely a tag is to produce a particular word. A verb might well be the word \"barks\".","words":[{"w":"Emission","start":69.754},{"w":"chances:","start":70.314},{"w":"how","start":71.074},{"w":"likely","start":71.354},{"w":"a","start":71.754},{"w":"tag","start":71.914},{"w":"is","start":72.274},{"w":"to","start":72.394},{"w":"produce","start":72.554},{"w":"a","start":72.954},{"w":"particular","start":73.074},{"w":"word.","start":73.714},{"w":"A","start":74.047},{"w":"verb","start":74.381},{"w":"might","start":74.714},{"w":"well","start":74.954},{"w":"be","start":75.154},{"w":"the","start":75.314},{"w":"word","start":75.474},{"w":"\"barks\".","start":75.754}]}],"title":"Two kinds of chances","shortTitle":"Two kinds of chances","props":{"kicker":"What it learns","title":"Two kinds of chances","columns":[{"title":"Transition","items":["tag → next tag","after DET, a NOUN is likely","count pairs of tags"],"tone":"neutral"},{"title":"Emission","items":["tag → word","a VERB may well be “barks”","count tag-and-word pairs"],"tone":"neutral"}]},"start":56.5,"end":76.273,"startFrame":1695,"durationInFrames":621},{"id":"example","kind":"core","component":"Table","short":true,"cues":[{"id":"c10","start":77.2,"end":78.973,"marks":{},"text":"Let's tag \"the dog barks\".","words":[{"w":"Let's","start":77.2},{"w":"tag","start":77.52},{"w":"\"the","start":77.92},{"w":"dog","start":78.08},{"w":"barks\".","start":78.44}]},{"id":"c11","start":79.373,"end":81.125,"marks":{},"text":"\"The\" can only be a determiner.","words":[{"w":"\"The\"","start":79.493},{"w":"can","start":79.613},{"w":"only","start":79.813},{"w":"be","start":80.093},{"w":"a","start":80.293},{"w":"determiner.","start":80.413}]},{"id":"c12","start":81.525,"end":90.367,"marks":{},"text":"\"Dog\" could be a noun, or a verb, as in \"to dog someone's steps\". But a noun is far more likely after a determiner, so the model picks noun.","words":[{"w":"\"Dog\"","start":81.525},{"w":"could","start":81.965},{"w":"be","start":82.085},{"w":"a","start":82.245},{"w":"noun,","start":82.365},{"w":"or","start":82.765},{"w":"a","start":83.085},{"w":"verb,","start":83.405},{"w":"as","start":83.725},{"w":"in","start":83.965},{"w":"\"to","start":84.205},{"w":"dog","start":84.485},{"w":"someone's","start":84.845},{"w":"steps\".","start":85.405},{"w":"But","start":86.005},{"w":"a","start":86.245},{"w":"noun","start":86.405},{"w":"is","start":86.805},{"w":"far","start":86.965},{"w":"more","start":87.205},{"w":"likely","start":87.485},{"w":"after","start":87.885},{"w":"a","start":88.125},{"w":"determiner,","start":88.245},{"w":"so","start":88.925},{"w":"the","start":89.125},{"w":"model","start":89.285},{"w":"picks","start":89.645},{"w":"noun.","start":89.965}]},{"id":"c13","start":90.767,"end":98.518,"marks":{},"text":"\"Barks\" could be a noun too, the bark of a tree, in the plural. But after a noun, a verb fits much better. So the best guess is verb.","words":[{"w":"\"Barks\"","start":90.767},{"w":"could","start":91.207},{"w":"be","start":91.327},{"w":"a","start":91.514},{"w":"noun","start":91.7},{"w":"too,","start":91.887},{"w":"the","start":92.127},{"w":"bark","start":92.287},{"w":"of","start":92.607},{"w":"a","start":92.727},{"w":"tree,","start":92.847},{"w":"in","start":93.207},{"w":"the","start":93.327},{"w":"plural.","start":93.487},{"w":"But","start":94.047},{"w":"after","start":94.367},{"w":"a","start":94.687},{"w":"noun,","start":94.807},{"w":"a","start":95.127},{"w":"verb","start":95.447},{"w":"fits","start":95.767},{"w":"much","start":96.207},{"w":"better.","start":96.447},{"w":"So","start":96.887},{"w":"the","start":97.087},{"w":"best","start":97.287},{"w":"guess","start":97.595},{"w":"is","start":97.903},{"w":"verb.","start":98.21}]}],"title":"A worked example","shortTitle":"How AI tags “the dog barks”","props":{"kicker":"Worked example","title":"“the dog barks”","columns":["Word","Could be","Best guess"],"rows":[["the","DET","DET"],["dog","NOUN · VERB","NOUN"],["barks","NOUN · VERB","VERB"]],"highlight":[{"row":1,"col":2},{"row":2,"col":2}]},"start":77.2,"end":98.518,"startFrame":2316,"durationInFrames":667},{"id":"viterbi","kind":"core","component":"Steps","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c14","start":99.433,"end":107.155,"marks":{},"text":"How does the model find the best tags for a whole sentence? It uses a clever method called the Viterbi algorithm, in four steps.","words":[{"w":"How","start":99.433},{"w":"does","start":99.553},{"w":"the","start":99.793},{"w":"model","start":99.913},{"w":"find","start":100.313},{"w":"the","start":100.553},{"w":"best","start":100.713},{"w":"tags","start":100.993},{"w":"for","start":101.473},{"w":"a","start":101.633},{"w":"whole","start":101.793},{"w":"sentence?","start":102.073},{"w":"It","start":102.793},{"w":"uses","start":103.113},{"w":"a","start":103.513},{"w":"clever","start":103.633},{"w":"method","start":103.953},{"w":"called","start":104.313},{"w":"the","start":104.593},{"w":"Viterbi","start":104.953},{"w":"algorithm,","start":105.313},{"w":"in","start":106.073},{"w":"four","start":106.313},{"w":"steps.","start":106.593}]},{"id":"c15","start":107.555,"end":110.713,"marks":{},"text":"Start: for the first word, score every tag it could have.","words":[{"w":"Start:","start":107.555},{"w":"for","start":107.995},{"w":"the","start":108.155},{"w":"first","start":108.275},{"w":"word,","start":108.635},{"w":"score","start":108.995},{"w":"every","start":109.475},{"w":"tag","start":109.715},{"w":"it","start":110.035},{"w":"could","start":110.235},{"w":"have.","start":110.475}]},{"id":"c16","start":111.113,"end":118.118,"marks":{},"text":"Extend: for each next word, and for each possible tag, keep only the single best path that leads into that tag.","words":[{"w":"Extend:","start":111.113},{"w":"for","start":111.793},{"w":"each","start":112.073},{"w":"next","start":112.393},{"w":"word,","start":112.793},{"w":"and","start":113.033},{"w":"for","start":113.233},{"w":"each","start":113.433},{"w":"possible","start":113.673},{"w":"tag,","start":114.313},{"w":"keep","start":114.873},{"w":"only","start":115.193},{"w":"the","start":115.473},{"w":"single","start":115.673},{"w":"best","start":116.113},{"w":"path","start":116.433},{"w":"that","start":116.713},{"w":"leads","start":116.913},{"w":"into","start":117.273},{"w":"that","start":117.513},{"w":"tag.","start":117.713}]},{"id":"c17","start":118.518,"end":121.665,"marks":{},"text":"Finish: at the last word, pick the tag with the best path.","words":[{"w":"Finish:","start":118.518},{"w":"at","start":119.038},{"w":"the","start":119.198},{"w":"last","start":119.398},{"w":"word,","start":119.718},{"w":"pick","start":120.038},{"w":"the","start":120.318},{"w":"tag","start":120.438},{"w":"with","start":120.758},{"w":"the","start":120.918},{"w":"best","start":121.038},{"w":"path.","start":121.358}]},{"id":"c18","start":122.065,"end":126.967,"marks":{},"text":"Trace back: follow that winning path backwards, and you have the best tag for every word.","words":[{"w":"Trace","start":122.065},{"w":"back:","start":122.545},{"w":"follow","start":122.945},{"w":"that","start":123.225},{"w":"winning","start":123.425},{"w":"path","start":123.785},{"w":"backwards,","start":124.145},{"w":"and","start":124.745},{"w":"you","start":124.945},{"w":"have","start":125.145},{"w":"the","start":125.305},{"w":"best","start":125.425},{"w":"tag","start":125.745},{"w":"for","start":126.105},{"w":"every","start":126.305},{"w":"word.","start":126.665}]}],"title":"The Viterbi algorithm","shortTitle":"The Viterbi algorithm","props":{"kicker":"Finding the best tags","title":"The Viterbi algorithm","steps":[{"label":"Start","detail":"which tags fit the first word?"},{"label":"Extend","detail":"best path into each tag, word by word"},{"label":"Finish","detail":"pick the best last tag"},{"label":"Trace back","detail":"follow that path backwards"}]},"start":99.433,"end":126.967,"startFrame":2983,"durationInFrames":854},{"id":"fast","kind":"core","component":"Bullets","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c19","start":127.9,"end":129.241,"marks":{},"text":"Why go to this trouble?","words":[{"w":"Why","start":127.9},{"w":"go","start":128.14},{"w":"to","start":128.38},{"w":"this","start":128.54},{"w":"trouble?","start":128.78}]},{"id":"c20","start":129.641,"end":138.502,"marks":{},"text":"Because trying every combination of tags is hopeless. With ten words and a dozen tags each, there are more combinations than there are people on Earth.","words":[{"w":"Because","start":129.641},{"w":"trying","start":129.961},{"w":"every","start":130.441},{"w":"combination","start":130.761},{"w":"of","start":131.321},{"w":"tags","start":131.481},{"w":"is","start":131.961},{"w":"hopeless.","start":132.201},{"w":"With","start":132.921},{"w":"ten","start":133.241},{"w":"words","start":133.601},{"w":"and","start":133.961},{"w":"a","start":134.161},{"w":"dozen","start":134.281},{"w":"tags","start":134.641},{"w":"each,","start":135.121},{"w":"there","start":135.481},{"w":"are","start":135.721},{"w":"more","start":135.961},{"w":"combinations","start":136.201},{"w":"than","start":137.081},{"w":"there","start":137.241},{"w":"are","start":137.481},{"w":"people","start":137.641},{"w":"on","start":137.961},{"w":"Earth.","start":138.161}]},{"id":"c21","start":138.902,"end":144.208,"marks":{},"text":"Viterbi keeps only the best path into each tag at each word, and throws the rest away.","words":[{"w":"Viterbi","start":139.262},{"w":"keeps","start":139.622},{"w":"only","start":140.022},{"w":"the","start":140.182},{"w":"best","start":140.342},{"w":"path","start":140.622},{"w":"into","start":140.942},{"w":"each","start":141.182},{"w":"tag","start":141.462},{"w":"at","start":141.822},{"w":"each","start":142.022},{"w":"word,","start":142.342},{"w":"and","start":142.662},{"w":"throws","start":142.942},{"w":"the","start":143.342},{"w":"rest","start":143.542},{"w":"away.","start":143.862}]},{"id":"c22","start":144.608,"end":150.382,"marks":{},"text":"So the work grows gently with the length of the sentence, and even long sentences stay quick to tag.","words":[{"w":"So","start":144.608},{"w":"the","start":144.728},{"w":"work","start":144.888},{"w":"grows","start":145.168},{"w":"gently","start":145.568},{"w":"with","start":146.008},{"w":"the","start":146.168},{"w":"length","start":146.288},{"w":"of","start":146.648},{"w":"the","start":146.768},{"w":"sentence,","start":146.928},{"w":"and","start":147.568},{"w":"even","start":147.848},{"w":"long","start":148.248},{"w":"sentences","start":148.528},{"w":"stay","start":148.955},{"w":"quick","start":149.381},{"w":"to","start":149.808},{"w":"tag.","start":149.968}]}],"title":"Why it's fast","shortTitle":"Why it's fast","props":{"kicker":"Why it matters","title":"Why Viterbi is so useful","items":[{"text":"Trying every combination of tags is hopeless"},{"text":"Viterbi keeps only the best path into each tag"},{"text":"So long sentences stay quick to tag"}],"numbered":false},"start":127.9,"end":150.382,"startFrame":3837,"durationInFrames":702},{"id":"limits","kind":"core","component":"Compare","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c23","start":151.3,"end":152.986,"marks":{},"text":"So how good are HMMs?","words":[{"w":"So","start":151.3},{"w":"how","start":151.46},{"w":"good","start":151.66},{"w":"are","start":151.86},{"w":"HMMs?","start":152.423}]},{"id":"c24","start":153.386,"end":159.232,"marks":{},"text":"Their strengths: they're simple, fast, learn just by counting, and make a strong baseline for tagging.","words":[{"w":"Their","start":153.386},{"w":"strengths:","start":153.626},{"w":"they're","start":154.106},{"w":"simple,","start":154.586},{"w":"fast,","start":155.186},{"w":"learn","start":155.706},{"w":"just","start":156.066},{"w":"by","start":156.306},{"w":"counting,","start":156.546},{"w":"and","start":156.986},{"w":"make","start":157.226},{"w":"a","start":157.426},{"w":"strong","start":157.546},{"w":"baseline","start":158.046},{"w":"for","start":158.546},{"w":"tagging.","start":158.706}]},{"id":"c25","start":159.632,"end":176.382,"marks":{},"text":"Their limits: each step only looks at the previous tag, and it's awkward to add extra clues, like a word's spelling or capital letters. And as a generative model, it spends effort modelling the words themselves, when we only need the tags. Next lesson's model lifts these limits.","words":[{"w":"Their","start":159.632},{"w":"limits:","start":159.872},{"w":"each","start":160.512},{"w":"step","start":160.912},{"w":"only","start":161.272},{"w":"looks","start":161.552},{"w":"at","start":161.792},{"w":"the","start":161.912},{"w":"previous","start":162.032},{"w":"tag,","start":162.512},{"w":"and","start":162.912},{"w":"it's","start":163.152},{"w":"awkward","start":163.352},{"w":"to","start":163.792},{"w":"add","start":163.912},{"w":"extra","start":164.232},{"w":"clues,","start":164.632},{"w":"like","start":165.072},{"w":"a","start":165.312},{"w":"word's","start":165.512},{"w":"spelling","start":165.712},{"w":"or","start":166.272},{"w":"capital","start":166.512},{"w":"letters.","start":167.032},{"w":"And","start":167.632},{"w":"as","start":167.912},{"w":"a","start":168.112},{"w":"generative","start":168.472},{"w":"model,","start":168.832},{"w":"it","start":169.272},{"w":"spends","start":169.472},{"w":"effort","start":169.872},{"w":"modelling","start":170.272},{"w":"the","start":170.752},{"w":"words","start":170.912},{"w":"themselves,","start":171.272},{"w":"when","start":171.912},{"w":"we","start":172.112},{"w":"only","start":172.352},{"w":"need","start":172.592},{"w":"the","start":172.912},{"w":"tags.","start":173.072},{"w":"Next","start":173.659},{"w":"lesson's","start":174.245},{"w":"model","start":174.832},{"w":"lifts","start":175.232},{"w":"these","start":175.592},{"w":"limits.","start":175.832}]}],"title":"Strengths and limits","shortTitle":"Strengths and limits","props":{"kicker":"Pros and cons","title":"Strengths and limits","columns":[{"title":"Strengths","items":["simple and fast","learns just by counting","a strong baseline for tagging"],"tone":"good"},{"title":"Limits","items":["sees only the previous tag","hard to add clues like spelling","spends effort modelling the words"],"tone":"bad"}],"verdict":{"text":"Next lesson: CRFs lift these limits"}},"start":151.3,"end":176.382,"startFrame":4539,"durationInFrames":780},{"id":"quiz","kind":"quiz","component":"Quiz","short":true,"cues":[{"id":"c26","start":177.3,"end":184.08,"marks":{},"text":"Quick quiz. In a hidden Markov model used for tagging, what is hidden: the words, the tags, or the sentence length?","words":[{"w":"Quick","start":177.527},{"w":"quiz.","start":177.753},{"w":"In","start":177.98},{"w":"a","start":178.14},{"w":"hidden","start":178.26},{"w":"Markov","start":178.66},{"w":"model","start":179.06},{"w":"used","start":179.42},{"w":"for","start":179.66},{"w":"tagging,","start":179.78},{"w":"what","start":180.34},{"w":"is","start":180.58},{"w":"hidden:","start":180.78},{"w":"the","start":181.38},{"w":"words,","start":181.7},{"w":"the","start":182.22},{"w":"tags,","start":182.42},{"w":"or","start":182.94},{"w":"the","start":183.14},{"w":"sentence","start":183.3},{"w":"length?","start":183.78}]},{"id":"c27","start":184.48,"end":186,"marks":{},"text":"Pause the video and choose.","words":[{"w":"Pause","start":184.48},{"w":"the","start":184.76},{"w":"video","start":185.02},{"w":"and","start":185.28},{"w":"choose.","start":185.48}]},{"id":"c28","start":189.4,"end":195.047,"marks":{},"text":"It's the tags. We can see the words. The tags are the hidden states the model is trying to guess.","words":[{"w":"It's","start":189.4},{"w":"the","start":189.64},{"w":"tags.","start":189.8},{"w":"We","start":190.4},{"w":"can","start":190.6},{"w":"see","start":190.84},{"w":"the","start":191.08},{"w":"words.","start":191.24},{"w":"The","start":191.88},{"w":"tags","start":192.12},{"w":"are","start":192.64},{"w":"the","start":192.76},{"w":"hidden","start":192.88},{"w":"states","start":193.24},{"w":"the","start":193.56},{"w":"model","start":193.72},{"w":"is","start":194.08},{"w":"trying","start":194.2},{"w":"to","start":194.48},{"w":"guess.","start":194.64}]}],"title":"Quick quiz","shortTitle":"Quick quiz: what's hidden in a Hidden Markov Model?","props":{"kicker":"Pause and predict","question":"In an HMM used for tagging, what is hidden?","options":["The words","The tags","The sentence length"],"answer":1,"explain":"We see the words; the tags are the hidden states we're trying to guess."},"start":177.3,"end":195.047,"startFrame":5319,"durationInFrames":560},{"id":"recap","kind":"recap","component":"Recap","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c29","start":195.967,"end":200.53,"marks":{},"text":"Let's recap. In an HMM, hidden tags produce the words we can see.","words":[{"w":"Let's","start":195.967},{"w":"recap.","start":196.327},{"w":"In","start":196.927},{"w":"an","start":197.354},{"w":"HMM,","start":197.78},{"w":"hidden","start":198.207},{"w":"tags","start":198.607},{"w":"produce","start":199.007},{"w":"the","start":199.367},{"w":"words","start":199.527},{"w":"we","start":199.847},{"w":"can","start":200.007},{"w":"see.","start":200.247}]},{"id":"c30","start":200.93,"end":205.202,"marks":{},"text":"Transition chances say how likely one tag is to follow another.","words":[{"w":"Transition","start":200.93},{"w":"chances","start":201.61},{"w":"say","start":202.29},{"w":"how","start":202.57},{"w":"likely","start":202.85},{"w":"one","start":203.25},{"w":"tag","start":203.49},{"w":"is","start":203.97},{"w":"to","start":204.17},{"w":"follow","start":204.37},{"w":"another.","start":204.77}]},{"id":"c31","start":205.602,"end":209.299,"marks":{},"text":"Emission chances say how likely a tag is to produce a word.","words":[{"w":"Emission","start":205.602},{"w":"chances","start":206.082},{"w":"say","start":206.642},{"w":"how","start":206.882},{"w":"likely","start":207.082},{"w":"a","start":207.482},{"w":"tag","start":207.602},{"w":"is","start":208.042},{"w":"to","start":208.242},{"w":"produce","start":208.402},{"w":"a","start":208.842},{"w":"word.","start":208.962}]},{"id":"c32","start":209.699,"end":214.165,"marks":{},"text":"And the Viterbi algorithm finds the best tags for a whole sentence, quickly.","words":[{"w":"And","start":209.699},{"w":"the","start":209.779},{"w":"Viterbi","start":209.899},{"w":"algorithm","start":210.419},{"w":"finds","start":211.139},{"w":"the","start":211.459},{"w":"best","start":211.619},{"w":"tags","start":211.899},{"w":"for","start":212.299},{"w":"a","start":212.419},{"w":"whole","start":212.579},{"w":"sentence,","start":213.108},{"w":"quickly.","start":213.636}]},{"id":"c33","start":214.565,"end":218.587,"marks":{},"text":"Next lesson: CRFs. How can a tagger use many clues at once?","words":[{"w":"Next","start":215.005},{"w":"lesson:","start":215.445},{"w":"CRFs.","start":215.885},{"w":"How","start":216.325},{"w":"can","start":216.605},{"w":"a","start":216.805},{"w":"tagger","start":217.045},{"w":"use","start":217.285},{"w":"many","start":217.525},{"w":"clues","start":217.725},{"w":"at","start":218.085},{"w":"once?","start":218.245}]}],"title":"Recap and next lesson","shortTitle":"Recap and next lesson","props":{"title":"Recap","points":["Hidden tags produce the words we see","Transition chances: tag to next tag","Emission chances: tag to word","Viterbi finds the best tags quickly"],"next":{"title":"CRFs","question":"How can a tagger use many clues at once?"}},"start":195.967,"end":218.587,"startFrame":5879,"durationInFrames":724}],"refs":{"c01":0.6,"c02":7.461,"c03":17.867,"c04":29.567,"c05":38.754,"c06":45.938,"c07":56.5,"c08":61.731,"c09":69.754,"c10":77.2,"c11":79.373,"c12":81.525,"c13":90.767,"c14":99.433,"c15":107.555,"c16":111.113,"c17":118.518,"c18":122.065,"c19":127.9,"c20":129.641,"c21":138.902,"c22":144.608,"c23":151.3,"c24":153.386,"c25":159.632,"c26":177.3,"c27":184.48,"c28":189.4,"c29":195.967,"c30":200.93,"c31":205.602,"c32":209.699,"c33":214.565},"audio":[{"file":".cache/proc/a9699eae7927f209.wav","start":0.6},{"file":".cache/proc/bdf2af7b210edbd9.wav","start":7.461},{"file":".cache/proc/6c5941d383107990.wav","start":17.867},{"file":".cache/proc/dc7020ecee64cec7.wav","start":29.567},{"file":".cache/proc/660afa5f943e26e1.wav","start":38.754},{"file":".cache/proc/65dc6e7c6a002a99.wav","start":45.938},{"file":".cache/proc/f9dc8725610fcf94.wav","start":56.5},{"file":".cache/proc/88755e31